ata-ref="8100c37c-172e-4a98-9214-648f1906fee1" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="70d3c8b1-0a50-473b-a5d0-8a5b16623418"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="4915fcc0-5896-4498-af4a-40b26acfecc1"><p data-ref="e2f80e27-cc4a-4c39-ae5e-207bfa9525f3" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a Python program that defines a base class <strong data-ref="244373e3-4c9b-475b-ac43-b163ddefad5a">Shape</strong> with two methods, <strong data-ref="dad471df-f24d-48f6-af66-c29d00181835">area</strong> and <strong data-ref="40a926dd-4453-4212-b354-caf2ac99bc0a">perimeter</strong>, that are meant to be overridden by subclasses. Define three subclasses: <strong data-ref="bcd02c00-b670-4554-8f38-087203617ee3">Circle</strong>, <strong data-ref="2f64480f-a875-4103-beb3-a0738334b96e">Triangle</strong>, and <strong data-ref="6ec5e5d7-fb9b-4041-a33e-6d1aac06a598">Square</strong>, each of which implements the <strong data-ref="77c17f9a-f5be-4f69-88e3-c007dd4f08bc">area</strong> and <strong data-ref="893167e2-2f60-465c-8183-c314e9eb4f6e">perimeter</strong> methods. The program should then create instances of these subclasses based on user input and print their areas and perimeters, formatted to two decimal places.</p><p data-ref="091cec6d-7520-421c-a6ea-23635e22fa22" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="3db97129-19b7-4c4f-97e1-07cb7c15e579"></p><p data-ref="43f339f5-89f6-4254-b5ec-080fc62a63a3" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="bcc0ab6a-b004-4daf-b837-ed6cc2114f2b">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="8ae1c436-3533-4ec6-bf1f-4f1e15376aff" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="7e5b0145-511c-497d-b92d-b8baf93a4300">The first line contains a single float representing the radius of a circle.</li><li data-ref="d843622e-a9cb-46c3-a60c-28c09ed827bf">The second line contains three space-separated floats representing the sides of a triangle.</li><li data-ref="c39d4738-a381-471d-9141-09dbc9e2a088">The third line contains a single float representing the side length of a square.</li></ul><p data-ref="1d015298-94e0-4136-b5e7-34a8d096f186" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="0fdfe1ca-177a-429d-9b86-7d39aca453f1"></p><p data-ref="2b58164c-4952-4f8d-8d7d-537fd5304aba" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter